# A function whose value is used says what it gives back (principle `gives`): the shortcut's `get_store()` says
# nothing, so what it gives is a value of no type and the `history` the route calls on it is a call no one can follow.
# The route builds a store from what the environment holds and reaches no table: the gap is the finding.

route harvest.api.readings
step readings/get_store
step readings/get_store/ReadingStore()
step readings/get_store().history                             # the call on what get_store gave, not followed

line entry > readings call
line Global(os.environ) > readings/get_store own              # os.environ.get(..), its result handed straight to ReadingStore()
line readings/get_store/ReadingStore() > ReadingStore@readings/get_store/ReadingStore() value
line ReadingStore@readings/get_store/ReadingStore() > readings/get_store value   # get_store hands back what it built
line readings/get_store > _@readings/get_store value          # what get_store gives has no type
line _@readings/get_store > readings/get_store().history value
line readings/get_store().history > readings back  # and what is asked of it goes back to the route, which returns it

home ReadingStore@readings/get_store/ReadingStore() readings/get_store
home _@readings/get_store readings

side entry left
side Global(os.environ) left
